1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,233
This is a tic-tac-toe game on the Midnight
blockchain.

2
00:00:03,233 --> 00:00:04,969
But it plays at memory speed.

3
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:09,274
Normally, every move would be a separate
blockchain transaction.

4
00:00:09,274 --> 00:00:11,455
That's about twenty-five seconds each.

5
00:00:11,455 --> 00:00:13,866
A nine-move game would take three minutes.

6
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,383
Instead, we move the gameplay off-chain.

7
00:00:17,383 --> 00:00:20,244
On the left, player X is deploying the
contract.

8
00:00:20,244 --> 00:00:25,726
They submit only their own Merkle root — a
commitment to all the moves they might
ever make.

9
00:00:25,726 --> 00:00:28,050
The channel opens in a half-open state.

10
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,333
On the right, player O pastes the contract
address and submits their own commitments
from their own browser.

11
00:00:36,333 --> 00:00:38,268
Two transactions, one per player.

12
00:00:38,268 --> 00:00:41,317
Neither side can substitute the other's
commitments.

13
00:00:41,317 --> 00:00:42,725
The channel is now live.

14
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:45,958
From here, the chain goes quiet.

15
00:00:45,958 --> 00:00:50,426
Each move goes over a WebSocket — the
mover reveals one Merkle-tree leaf,

16
00:00:50,426 --> 00:00:53,242
and the opponent verifies it against the
root.

17
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:57,055
X completes the diagonal. The local game
ends.

18
00:00:57,055 --> 00:00:59,512
Now X submits one settle transaction.

19
00:00:59,512 --> 00:01:06,218
The contract replays every move and
verifies every token's Merkle path under
the right player's root.

20
00:01:06,218 --> 00:01:08,211
One proof, for the whole game.

21
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:13,855
Settle lands.

22
00:01:13,855 --> 00:01:17,998
The chain now records five committed turns
and X as the winner.

23
00:01:17,998 --> 00:01:24,378
A short challenge window opens — during
which a longer, valid history could
override this result.

24
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:26,396
The window expires.

25
00:01:26,396 --> 00:01:27,865
X claims the result.

26
00:01:27,865 --> 00:01:29,040
Status: settled.

27
00:01:29,500 --> 00:01:31,579
One game. Four chain transactions.

28
00:01:31,579 --> 00:01:33,169
The rest, at memory speed.

